// Config-Secrets.example.xcconfig
// ChristmasTracker — Sentry DSN secrets template
//
// Copy this file to Config-Secrets.xcconfig (same directory, next to
// ChristmasTracker.xcodeproj) and fill in your real Sentry DSN.
// Config-Secrets.xcconfig is gitignored and must never be committed.
//
// Why the https:/$()/... syntax:
//   xcconfig treats // as the start of a comment, so a bare Sentry DSN
//   (https://PUBLIC_KEY@HOST/PROJECT_ID) would be truncated to "https:".
//   Writing https:/$()/... expands the empty variable $() to "" at build
//   time, producing the correct https:// in the built app's Info.plist.
//
// Example (replace all-caps tokens with your real values):
SENTRY_DSN_RELEASE = https:/$()/PUBLIC_KEY@HOST/PROJECT_ID
